.IX Title "GENPYT 1"
.TH GENPYT 1 2024-07-13 "perl v5.38.2" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
genpyt \- generate the PINYIN lexicon
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBgenpyt\fR \fIlexicon-file\fR \fIresult-file\fR \fIlog-file\fR \fIslm-file\fR
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBgenpyt\fR is used to generate the PINYIN lexicon. 
It only works on zh_CN.UTF\-8 locale.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IX Header "ARGUMENTS"
.IP \fIlexicon-file\fR 4
.IX Item "lexicon-file"
Specify a dictionary file. It should be a line-based text file in utf\-8 encoding
\&. Each line looks like:
.Sp
.Vb 1
\&   CCC  id  [pinyin\*(Aqpinyin\*(Aqpinyin]*
.Ve
.Sp
A default dictionary file can be found at \fI/usr/share/sunpinyin/dict.utf8\fR.
.IP \fIresult-file\fR 4
.IX Item "result-file"
The output binary PINYIN lexicon file. This lexicon contains a trie presenting the key tree of PINYIN. And all of the candidate words are sorted using the unigram in \fIslm-file\fR. This file can be used with sunpinyin input method engines.
.IP \fIlog-file\fR 4
.IX Item "log-file"
Specify the file to where the log goes. The \fIlog-file\fR can be seen as the human-readble presentation of the binary output file.
.IP \fIslm-file\fR 4
.IX Item "slm-file"
The language model from which the unigram information are retrieved. Typically, the \fIslm-file\fR is generated by \fBslmthread\fR.
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Originally written by Phill.Zhang <phill.zhang@sun.com>.
Currently maintained by Kov.Chai <tchaikov@gmail.com>.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBslmthread\fR(1).
